# The Behavioral and Social Sciences Survey: Economics.

**Authors:** Ruggles, Nancy D., Ed.

## Abstract
This is one of a series in the Survey of the Behavioral and Social Sciences (BASS) conducted between 1967 and 1969. Three chapters of a general nature discuss the concerns of economists, professional organization, and research procedures (simulation, modeling, data needs, survey research, behavioral research, operations research), and the recommendations of the study committee. The remaining chapters are contributions by individual scholars on some specific subfields of economics, such as theory, econometrics, labor economics, urban economics, agricultural economics, the public sector, development, and international economics. (CWB)

